# Line endings are LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with the default core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# every text file to CRLF. That turned two gates red that are green on CI:
#
#   * `prettier --check` (its endOfLine default is "lf"), and
#   * src/policy/policy.test.ts, which compares the generated policy PDF
#     byte-for-byte against the committed fixture.
#
# Every blob in this repository is already LF, so this rule changes no content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A text-based PDF must never be line-ending converted. The xref table stores
# byte offsets, so adding a byte to every line corrupts the file: the committed
# health policy declares startxref 5473, and a CRLF checkout moves it to 5711.
*.pdf binary

# Generated fixtures are compared as data, not as source, and are rewritten by
# `npm run seed`. Leave their bytes alone.
fixtures/** -text
